{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25146238",
      "title": "Adding Markdown Files As A Data Source",
      "lectureOrder": 365,
      "videoOrder": 337,
      "sourceHash": "342b8a5283fac2489dcc8be2061af500e1684d6a5be3ac58f746746e48606809",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.409,
          "end": 3.34,
          "en": "So it's time to move away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.34,
          "end": 5.63,
          "en": "from those dummy posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.63,
          "end": 8.26,
          "en": "That of course, brings up one question,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.26,
          "end": 12.32,
          "en": "where do we wanna store our actual posts?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.32,
          "end": 16.61,
          "en": "And one pretty obvious choice would be a database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.61,
          "end": 21.61,
          "en": "something like Firebase or a MongoDB or SQL database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.73,
          "end": 23.81,
          "en": "And there is nothing wrong with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.81,
          "end": 27.19,
          "en": "We could do that, but for a blog like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.19,
          "end": 31.67,
          "en": "which is owned by us, where we write those blog posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.67,
          "end": 35.55,
          "en": "there also is another very nice solution.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.55,
          "end": 39.91,
          "en": "We could use our file system as a data source",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.91,
          "end": 43.85,
          "en": "because we don't need to write to our blog posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.85,
          "end": 46.36,
          "en": "I mean, we have to write them at some point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.36,
          "end": 47.95,
          "en": "but then once they're done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.95,
          "end": 51.12,
          "en": "they are a data source from which we only fetch data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.12,
          "end": 53.86,
          "en": "We only use them to load blog posts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 53.86,
          "end": 55.06,
          "en": "users on the website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.06,
          "end": 57.78,
          "en": "can't interact with them to change them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.78,
          "end": 61.16,
          "en": "So once they exist, we might occasionally update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.16,
          "end": 62.35,
          "en": "But whenever we do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.35,
          "end": 66.12,
          "en": "we as an owner dive directly into those blog posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.12,
          "end": 69.2,
          "en": "but the files themselves are then only fetched",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.2,
          "end": 71.21000000000001,
          "en": "by our application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.21000000000001,
          "end": 75.82,
          "en": "So if we use our local file system here, our project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.82,
          "end": 79.62,
          "en": "we don't have to set up an extra database and pay for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 79.62,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "We don't have to do all that wire up work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 84.82,
          "en": "and that can be pretty nice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 84.82,
          "end": 86.76,
          "en": "And therefore, a quite common approach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 86.76,
          "end": 90.56,
          "en": "is to add a new folder in your project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.56,
          "end": 93.13,
          "en": "which could be named content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 93.13,
          "end": 94.7,
          "en": "but that name is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.7,
          "end": 98.24000000000001,
          "en": "It doesn't have to be named content and in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.24000000000001,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "we could have a sub folder named, posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 104.28999999999999,
          "en": "if we would have different kinds of content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.28999999999999,
          "end": 107.84,
          "en": "or if we don't have that, we get rid of that folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.84,
          "end": 110.50999999999999,
          "en": "and instead of a content post folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.50999999999999,
          "end": 113.723,
          "en": "we just directly add a post folder in the project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 115.05,
          "end": 116.43,
          "en": "Now, the idea is that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.43,
          "end": 120.36,
          "en": "in that post folder, we store our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.36,
          "end": 123.343,
          "en": "And what do I mean with store our posts?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.38,
          "end": 125.56,
          "en": "Well, keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.56,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "that we will write our posts with markdown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 131.503,
          "en": "so with that markdown syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.35,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "Hence I'll add a new file in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 139.203,
          "en": "let's say, the getting-started-with-nextjs.md file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 142.36,
          "end": 144.823,
          "en": "MD stands for markdown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.76,
          "end": 148.84,
          "en": "So this is a markdown file, which I added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 148.84,
          "end": 151.94,
          "en": "And in there, we can write markdown code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.94,
          "end": 155.35,
          "en": "You can also install extra extensions that help you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.35,
          "end": 157.32,
          "en": "with writing markdown code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.32,
          "end": 160.7,
          "en": "In visual studio code, if you search for markdown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.7,
          "end": 162.87,
          "en": "there you can install extra support,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 162.87,
          "end": 164.36,
          "en": "but I don't even have that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.36,
          "end": 166.44299999999998,
          "en": "I am happy to write it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.64,
          "end": 170.75,
          "en": "Now in here, we kind of write that markdown code like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.75,
          "end": 172.87,
          "en": "this is a title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.87,
          "end": 176.85,
          "en": "this is some regular text with a link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 178.22,
          "end": 182.023,
          "en": "That is something could write here as content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.48,
          "end": 185.51,
          "en": "However, if you take a closer look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.51,
          "end": 188.96,
          "en": "at our pages and our different components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 188.96,
          "end": 192.79,
          "en": "you might see that just content is not enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.79,
          "end": 195.96,
          "en": "We also rely on an excerpt and a date",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 195.96,
          "end": 200.96,
          "en": "and a title and image for outputting all our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.01,
          "end": 204.84,
          "en": "So we need to add metadata to our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.84,
          "end": 206.92000000000002,
          "en": "And the great thing about markdown,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 206.92000000000002,
          "end": 209.1,
          "en": "is that you can easily combine it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 209.1,
          "end": 213.41,
          "en": "with a concept called gray matter, which is just metadata.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.41,
          "end": 215.86,
          "en": "You add to your markdown file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 215.86,
          "end": 219.326,
          "en": "You add that by adding free dashes, opening and closing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 219.326,
          "end": 223.23,
          "en": "so to say, above your content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 223.23,
          "end": 224.89,
          "en": "So here we have free dashes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 224.89,
          "end": 227.61,
          "en": "and between those free dash separators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.61,
          "end": 230.32,
          "en": "we can add our metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.32,
          "end": 234.82,
          "en": "for this markdown file as key value pairs basically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 234.82,
          "end": 237.803,
          "en": "in Yaml format to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 239.19,
          "end": 241.14,
          "en": "And you can look up Yaml formats",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 241.14,
          "end": 243.37,
          "en": "to see what's allowed in here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 243.37,
          "end": 245.66,
          "en": "And for example, we can set a title here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 245.66,
          "end": 249.25,
          "en": "to, this is the post title,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 249.25,
          "end": 253.627,
          "en": "or in this case, probably getting started with nextjS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 264.58,
          "end": 268.088,
          "en": "And we can also wrap that in quotes to make it clear that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 268.088,
          "end": 270.22,
          "en": "that's a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 270.22,
          "end": 272.46,
          "en": "It's technically not always required",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 272.46,
          "end": 275.06,
          "en": "but can be required sometimes if Yaml",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 275.06,
          "end": 279.033,
          "en": "is not able to find out which data type it is otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 279.98,
          "end": 283.03,
          "en": "Here you could also add an author if you need that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 283.03,
          "end": 285.652,
          "en": "I don't have it in this block since it's only my blog",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 285.652,
          "end": 288.3,
          "en": "and I'm the only author of all those posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.3,
          "end": 290.6,
          "en": "but you could add a author field here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.6,
          "end": 292.763,
          "en": "and then fetch and render that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.81,
          "end": 296.04,
          "en": "Now what we'll need is a image though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 296.04,
          "end": 298.73,
          "en": "we will definitely need that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.73,
          "end": 301.79,
          "en": "And here I'll just have my getting-started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.378,
          "end": 306.64,
          "en": "nextjs.png image file here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 306.64,
          "end": 308.22,
          "en": "So this image file, which I added",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 308.22,
          "end": 311.34,
          "en": "in the images posts folder before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 311.34,
          "end": 314.37,
          "en": "And as a side note to connect everything correctly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 314.37,
          "end": 316.95,
          "en": "and use the already existing structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.95,
          "end": 318.87,
          "en": "in the public images folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318.87,
          "end": 320.01,
          "en": "you should make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 320.01,
          "end": 324.15,
          "en": "that your posts markdown file has a file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.15,
          "end": 327.61,
          "en": "that matches one of the folder names in that posts folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.61,
          "end": 329.3,
          "en": "in the images folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 329.3,
          "end": 332.15,
          "en": "because we'll then later connect all that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 332.15,
          "end": 335.40999999999997,
          "en": "such that we fetch the image we specify here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.40999999999997,
          "end": 338.04,
          "en": "from a equally named folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 338.04,
          "end": 340.92,
          "en": "in the public images posts folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 340.92,
          "end": 343.07,
          "en": "So you should make sure that this is equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 344.76,
          "end": 348.81,
          "en": "Then here, we can also add an excerpt",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 348.81,
          "end": 353.81,
          "en": "and I'll just quickly grab my dummy excerpt here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 353.90999999999997,
          "end": 356.08,
          "en": "which I wrote down before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 356.08,
          "end": 360.92,
          "en": "from the index.js file and add that as an excerpt here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 360.92,
          "end": 362.37,
          "en": "I didn't add a line break here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.37,
          "end": 366.17,
          "en": "That's just my IDE, which is kind of showing a line break.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 366.17,
          "end": 368.423,
          "en": "It's one long inline text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.25,
          "end": 373.84,
          "en": "And I will now also add a isFeatured key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.84,
          "end": 375.7,
          "en": "and set this to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 375.7,
          "end": 379.41,
          "en": "So Boolean values are also allowed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 379.41,
          "end": 381.13,
          "en": "We will then later use that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.13,
          "end": 385.223,
          "en": "for selecting just the featured posts for the starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 386.14,
          "end": 388.28,
          "en": "So that's now extra metadata",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 388.28,
          "end": 391.35,
          "en": "and that's the actual post content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 391.35,
          "end": 393.43,
          "en": "And we can write files like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.43,
          "end": 395.13,
          "en": "and we can also fetch data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 395.13,
          "end": 398.311,
          "en": "from such files and split it in metadata and content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 398.311,
          "end": 401.65,
          "en": "All of that is possible with ease",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 401.65,
          "end": 405.44,
          "en": "and therefore that will be our data source here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 405.44,
          "end": 409.44,
          "en": "So now with that, all save that markdown file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 409.44,
          "end": 410.87,
          "en": "And I will now also get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 410.87,
          "end": 414.93,
          "en": "of the other dummy post folders in the images folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 414.93,
          "end": 417.65999999999997,
          "en": "and just keep one of those folders around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 417.65999999999997,
          "end": 420.34,
          "en": "for that markdown file we just added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 420.34,
          "end": 425.25,
          "en": "And now the goal is to kind of use our posts folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
